{"vid":"str-vdAA6V4","source":"str-vdAA6V4.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":1.4,"txt":"I'm not ready to set my sights on a capital C"},{"t":4.6,"txt":"career. I look around and I see so many people who have"},{"t":7.8,"txt":"a big career and they're so unhappy."},{"t":11,"txt":"I feel like with my little C career and my little life"},{"t":14,"txt":"that I have, I feel like I get so much more meaning and"},{"t":17.4,"txt":"fulfillment on a day to day basis."},{"t":19.8,"txt":"My name is Eileen Tyrrell."},{"t":21.2,"txt":"I'm 26 years old and I live in New York City on 53K a"},{"t":25,"txt":"year. New York just has an energy to it that I"},{"t":34,"txt":"don't know if I've experienced anywhere else."},{"t":36.9,"txt":"Just feels electric when you're walking around."},{"t":39.9,"txt":"I commute into Brooklyn every day."},{"t":44.8,"txt":"I am the store manager at the bookstore,"},{"t":47.1,"txt":"and from that I make $45,000 a year."},{"t":50,"txt":"The remaining $8,000 comes from side jobs,"},{"t":53,"txt":"primarily freelance writing."},{"t":54.7,"txt":"I also do pet sitting and now I'm making money from"},{"t":57.6,"txt":"TikTok."},{"t":58.6,"txt":"Spend the day with me as a normal person living in New"},{"t":61.1,"txt":"York on about 50K a year."},{"t":63,"txt":"I want to show people that you don't need to be making"},{"t":65.3,"txt":"six figures to have a good life in New York."},{"t":67.6,"txt":"It does feel very romantic, and just getting to be"},{"t":70.7,"txt":"around books all day long and getting to talk to"},{"t":72.6,"txt":"customers about books and shelve books and see what"},{"t":75.2,"txt":"new books are coming out, is a very special job."},{"t":77.5,"txt":"It's the kind of job that maybe you wanted when you"},{"t":79.5,"txt":"were a little kid, and then you grew up and you"},{"t":81.4,"txt":"had to be funneled into the corporate pipeline or"},{"t":83.9,"txt":"whatever. Budgeting in New York can be hard."},{"t":90.8,"txt":"I make $53,000 a year, and people ask me all the"},{"t":94.6,"txt":"time how it's possible to live here on that income."},{"t":98.1,"txt":"I'm not going to lie. I'm not going to sugarcoat it."},{"t":100.3,"txt":"It's hard, but it's so worth it."},{"t":102.8,"txt":"Once or twice a week I'll meal prep multiple meals and"},{"t":105.7,"txt":"that will be my lunch for work."},{"t":107.5,"txt":"It's okay that I'm living on this tight budget."},{"t":110,"txt":"For me, it comes down to three things."},{"t":111.9,"txt":"I don't have a lot of debt."},{"t":113.4,"txt":"I have very reasonable rent and I don't spend a lot of"},{"t":117.4,"txt":"money. This is one of my staple meals."},{"t":120.5,"txt":"Ate so many of these that the dentist told me I had"},{"t":123,"txt":"five cavities. My parents pay for my phone bill."},{"t":127.4,"txt":"Thank you, mom and dad."},{"t":129.6,"txt":"Other than that, I pay for everything myself."},{"t":131.8,"txt":"However, I do have the safety net of knowing that"},{"t":135.4,"txt":"they would be able to help me if something were to go"},{"t":137.6,"txt":"wrong. This is my go to meal,"},{"t":139.2,"txt":"honestly, when I don't want to spend a lot of money. I"},{"t":141.4,"txt":"have about $3,000 in student loans,"},{"t":143.9,"txt":"so my monthly payment is very manageable."},{"t":146.7,"txt":"I pay off my credit cards every month."},{"t":148.8,"txt":"I have two of them and I will not let them roll over."},{"t":152,"txt":"I think my parents, and specifically my dad,"},{"t":154.8,"txt":"instilled such a fear in me of credit card debt that it"},{"t":158.8,"txt":"feels sacrilegious to ever let payments accumulate."},{"t":162.3,"txt":"I pay $1566 a month in rent that does not include"},{"t":166.2,"txt":"utilities. I live with two roommates,"},{"t":168.4,"txt":"so that is a lot to pay to have two roommates."},{"t":170.9,"txt":"But for Manhattan, that is a good deal."},{"t":174.6,"txt":"I just don't really spend a lot of money."},{"t":176.5,"txt":"I don't buy a lot of things."},{"t":178.6,"txt":"All of my furniture and most of my possessions are things"},{"t":181.9,"txt":"that I either brought with me from college or are"},{"t":185.4,"txt":"hand-me-downs that friends gave me."},{"t":187.6,"txt":"This puffer, someone left it at a party at my friend's"},{"t":191,"txt":"house. So this jacket was free."},{"t":192.9,"txt":"I kind of had to train myself to find hobbies and"},{"t":196.8,"txt":"interests that weren't related to spending money."},{"t":199.5,"txt":"That really helps when you're living on this type"},{"t":202,"txt":"of budget. I try to keep my dining out expenses low"},{"t":209.1,"txt":"because that adds up very quickly."},{"t":211.6,"txt":"However, I get a bacon, egg,"},{"t":213.3,"txt":"and cheese from my local deli probably once or twice"},{"t":215.5,"txt":"a week. Can I do a bacon, egg,"},{"t":217.1,"txt":"and cheese on a toasted everything bagel,"},{"t":218.9,"txt":"please? There are a couple expenses that I don't really"},{"t":222.7,"txt":"stress about. The first one is buying coffee every day."},{"t":226.2,"txt":"Going to a coffee shop and having a face to face"},{"t":228.5,"txt":"interaction is so underrated."},{"t":230.3,"txt":"Just a drip coffee with half and half."},{"t":232.3,"txt":"It's honestly a highlight of my day."},{"t":234.1,"txt":"It's absolutely worth the $4.50 that I pay for my"},{"t":237.7,"txt":"coffee every day. I think the idea that we should be"},{"t":240.6,"txt":"sacrificing these little expenses for the sake of an"},{"t":244.3,"txt":"extra $20, $30 a week, that's an idea that I"},{"t":247.4,"txt":"struggle with, because I think sometimes"},{"t":249,"txt":"those little expenses are tied to a sense of community"},{"t":252.4,"txt":"and a sense of greater purpose."},{"t":254.7,"txt":"I donate about $100 of my monthly budget to various"},{"t":259.4,"txt":"organizations."},{"t":260.6,"txt":"I want to give back to a city that gives me so much."},{"t":263.3,"txt":"I try to focus on local organizations,"},{"t":265.9,"txt":"food banks, and mutual aid, stuff like that."},{"t":273.4,"txt":"I have thought about the risks of living with this"},{"t":276.9,"txt":"little in savings, and to me,"},{"t":279.3,"txt":"at this moment in time, it's worth it."},{"t":281,"txt":"I'm comfortable taking that risk and hoping that things"},{"t":284.4,"txt":"are going to work out further down the line."},{"t":286.5,"txt":"A lot of people might view that as naive or financially"},{"t":290.4,"txt":"irresponsible, and that's okay."},{"t":297.9,"txt":"I grew up in the Chicago suburbs,"},{"t":299.9,"txt":"and I studied civil engineering at Iowa State"},{"t":302.8,"txt":"University. But about two years into my degree,"},{"t":305.7,"txt":"I remembered that I'm not really a math and science"},{"t":308.9,"txt":"person. I'm more of a language person,"},{"t":311.4,"txt":"I love books, I love reading and writing."},{"t":313.6,"txt":"At that point, I was already halfway"},{"t":315.2,"txt":"through the program, and so I figured I would"},{"t":316.9,"txt":"just stick it out because I had taken way too many math"},{"t":319.6,"txt":"classes at that point to give up."},{"t":321.4,"txt":"I started to develop a backup plan because I knew"},{"t":324.4,"txt":"that once I graduated, I was probably not going to"},{"t":327.2,"txt":"be pursuing a full time career in engineering."},{"t":330.4,"txt":"Once I graduated, I was ready for something"},{"t":332.8,"txt":"else. I was ready to try living somewhere that I had"},{"t":335.1,"txt":"never lived before."},{"t":341,"txt":"When I moved to New York, I had about $3,000 in"},{"t":344.1,"txt":"savings, and that was after I had paid for the moving"},{"t":346.6,"txt":"truck and for my first month of rent and the security"},{"t":349.4,"txt":"deposit. These are going to be so good."},{"t":351.6,"txt":"I knew I obviously needed a job."},{"t":354.3,"txt":"I did apply to a couple of engineering jobs and I"},{"t":357.3,"txt":"actually got an offer."},{"t":358.7,"txt":"It was $67,000 a year."},{"t":360.8,"txt":"Thank you. I thought about it and I ultimately turned"},{"t":364.1,"txt":"it down. I had just made a promise to myself that I"},{"t":367.5,"txt":"wasn't going to take a job just because it felt like"},{"t":371,"txt":"the natural step or the expected thing for me."},{"t":374.4,"txt":"I wanted a job that filled my cup every day."},{"t":376.6,"txt":"I didn't want a job that was going to require me to sit"},{"t":379.4,"txt":"at a desk and do work that ultimately wasn't meaningful"},{"t":382.4,"txt":"to me. It was from that decision that I ended up"},{"t":385,"txt":"first working in a bookstore."},{"t":387,"txt":"I always kind of pictured it as more of a stop gap job,"},{"t":390.3,"txt":"but I just fell in love with it."},{"t":391.9,"txt":"I didn't expect it to expand into what is now my full"},{"t":395.2,"txt":"time job, but that's how things go."},{"t":397.4,"txt":"I guess you never know what's right around the"},{"t":399.4,"txt":"corner. I'm pretty content with my life at the moment."},{"t":406.4,"txt":"I'm not yearning for anything else."},{"t":408.4,"txt":"I have a job that I love, I have a life that I love,"},{"t":410.9,"txt":"and the financial stability is not quite there."},{"t":414.3,"txt":"But for now, it's a trade off that I'm comfortable"},{"t":417.3,"txt":"with and I'm willing to make because I love my life so"},{"t":420.2,"txt":"much. There's this Oscar Wilde quote that goes"},{"t":423.7,"txt":"something like with freedom,"},{"t":425.4,"txt":"flowers, books and the moon,"},{"t":427,"txt":"how could one not be perfectly happy?"},{"t":429.3,"txt":"I have freedom, I can go buy flowers."},{"t":432.7,"txt":"Okay, sometimes I can't afford flowers,"},{"t":434.5,"txt":"but I have freedom and I have books and I have the"},{"t":438.2,"txt":"moon. And that is enough for me a lot of the times."}],"words":[{"t":1.36,"w":"I'm"},{"t":1.36,"w":"not"},{"t":1.36,"w":"ready"},{"t":1.36,"w":"to"},{"t":1.36,"w":"set"},{"t":1.36,"w":"my"},{"t":1.36,"w":"si